J-W061-B | check | the two bare leads stay 2.54 mm apart and touch nothing else (by eye); continuity test to the cell's can: open
    -> case step 10 (a), board unpowered, ohmmeter, black probe on test pad TP16 (GND), red probe on point T, the pad of RT2 that does not beep to TP16 (net TS): before TH1 is fitted the steady reading R0 is 29.8 to 30.4 kohm (RT2 alone, if the unpowered charger draws nothing; any steady R0 from 4.5 to 30.4 kohm is accepted); after the two joints the steady reading R1 is 6.4 to 10.1 kohm when R0 was 29.8 to 30.4 kohm (about 7.5 kohm at 25 C), and R0 x R1 / (R0 - R1), the thermistor alone, is 8.2 to 15.1 kohm at 15 to 30 C; the meter's path runs through TH1.1, the bead and TH1.2, so the reading proves both joints; R1 equal to R0 means a joint is open, near 0 ohm a short. By eye at 10 times: the two bare leads touch nothing else over their whole length. Last, with the cell in place: continuity from each lead to the cell's can: open (design/wiring/lead-decisions.md:71)
